# `node_modules` on its own matches only the context root — Docker does not
# apply bare patterns recursively. Every packages/*/node_modules was therefore
# still being sent, and `COPY packages/ packages/` (Dockerfile:33) dropped the
# host's symlink farm on top of the one `pnpm install` had just built inside
# the image. The build only ever succeeded when the host's node_modules
# happened to agree with the lockfile; run pnpm once on the host and the next
# from-scratch build fails with "Cannot find module .../rimraf/dist/esm/bin.mjs"
# or the same for tsc. `**/` makes it recursive and the build hermetic.
**/node_modules
.git
*.md
!README.md
packages/client/dist
packages/client/dist_injected
packages/client/playwright-report
packages/client/test-results
.mise
.vscode
.github
docs
